WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.259
Netflix is adding a bunch of awesome content
in July 2019 and getting rid of a lot of great

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.120
titles too.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.960
Here are our picks for the movies you have
to stream one more time before they leave

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:10.660
the service.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.760
In the mood for something swinging, shagadelic,
and downright groovy?

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.280
Netflix subscribers have until July 1st to
catch Mike Myers as the buck-toothed, babe-obsessed

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.560
British spy Austin Powers in the first two
films of his action-comedy franchise.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:27.770
Austin Powers: International Man of Mystery
centers on its titular spy as he wakes up

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:33.320
in 1997 after spending 30 years on ice following
an assassination attempt by Dr. Evil.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.220
Also played by Mike Myers, Dr. Evil soon concocts
a plan to hold a $100 billion ransom over

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:38.720
the world.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.800
"$100 billion!"

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.480
What comes next is a string of silly antics,
evil henchmen, beautiful "fembots," a Generation

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:51.810
X son with serious daddy issues, a doomsday
device, and plenty of James Bond gags.

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:55.649
Meanwhile, The Spy Who Shagged Me, takes everything
fans loved about the first film, then adds

00:00:55.649 --> 00:01:00.809
a clone, a time-traveling VW Beetle, a Scottish
Guard, and a volcano lair into the mix.

00:01:00.809 --> 00:01:04.300
If laughter is what you're after, an Austin
Powers double feature is just the thing for

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:04.800
you.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:10.380
The dark fantasy drama from Academy Award-winning
director Guillermo del Toro, Pan's Labyrinth

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:14.960
made it onto countless best-of-year lists
when it opened to sweeping acclaim in 2006.

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:19.200
In the 13 years since its release, the film
has been regarded as one of the greatest movies

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.220
of all time and the best of del Toro's illustrious
career.

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:27.280
Set in Spain in the summer of 1944, the film
follows Ofelia, a young girl who discovers

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.250
that she may be the living reincarnation of
a royal whose father ruled the underworld.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:35.740
One evening, Ofelia follows an insect she
believes to be a fairy into a labyrinth where

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.710
she meets the Faun, a being who tasks her
with three missions she must complete in order

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.610
to become immortal and live in the underworld
as a Princess.

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:46.189
Pan's Labyrinth leaves Netflix at the end
of June so enter the maze and discover its

00:01:46.189 --> 00:01:47.540
magic before it's too late.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:53.120
If you have yet to see director Jonathan Demme's
psychological horror film, July 1st is your

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.780
last chance to do so on Netflix.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:59.840
The Silence of the Lambs, an adaptation of
Thomas Harris' 1988 novel of the same name,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:04.150
follows ambitious young FBI trainee Clarice
Starling as she builds a relationship with

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:06.920
imprisoned cannibal serial killer Dr. Hannibal
Lecter.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.760
She needs his advice to catch another insane
serial killer, "Buffalo Bill."

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:14.859
Within the cold walls of the Baltimore State
Hospital for the Criminally Insane, Clarice

00:02:14.859 --> 00:02:18.999
offers personal information to Hannibal in
exchange for clues on the identity of Buffalo

00:02:18.999 --> 00:02:21.040
Bill and how she might apprehend him.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.790
One of the top-grossing movies of 1991, the
winner of multiple Academy Awards, a critical

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:30.189
and commercial success, and a film preserved
in the National Film Registry, The Silence

00:02:30.189 --> 00:02:33.389
of the Lambs is a cinema classic and a linchpin
of the thriller genre.

00:02:33.389 --> 00:02:36.389
Don't miss watching it from the comfort of
your couch while you still can.

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:38.780
There's no telling what Dr. Lecter might do
otherwise.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:43.020
A census taker once tried to test me.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:48.760
I ate his liver beans with some fava beans
and a nice glass of chianti."

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.540
If you're suffering from a serious case of
Keanu Reeves Fever, you'll want to watch The

00:02:53.549 --> 00:02:57.340
Matrix trilogy before Netflix clears the films
from its content library.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:02.340
First, dig into 1999's The Matrix, featuring
Reeves as computer programmer Thomas Anderson,

00:03:02.589 --> 00:03:04.720
who hides a double life as a hacker named
"Neo."

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:09.360
When he meets Morpheus, Neo's reality is forever
changed after he discovers that the reality

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.820
he knows is completely fabricated.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:15.499
Neo realizes that he's been trapped in the
Matrix, a system that presents a false reality

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.960
to its victims and feeds off their minds and
bodies.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.900
Once your brain has been thoroughly blown
by The Matrix, dive deeper into the stylish

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.540
world with The Matrix Reloaded and The Matrix
Revolutions.

00:03:25.609 --> 00:03:30.489
James Cameron's 1984 sci-fi flick The Terminator
is essential viewing for anyone who loves

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:36.159
cyborg assassins, Arnold Schwarzenegger, high-stakes
time-travel, and bombastic action sequences.

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:40.559
It's also a required watch leading up to the
premiere of November's Terminator: Dark Fate.

00:03:40.559 --> 00:03:44.299
As if you don't already know, the film features
Schwarzenegger as an android sent from the

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:48.140
year 2029 to 1984 Los Angeles to kill Sarah
Connor.

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:52.239
She'll eventually become the mother to the
man destined to save humankind from a sentient

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.740
artificial intelligence system known as Skynet.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:59.419
Meanwhile, a human soldier from the future,
Kyle Reese, risks everything to protect Sarah

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.520
from being terminated.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.480
Whether you're reliving the action or witnessing
it for the first time, catching The Terminator

00:04:04.489 --> 00:04:07.930
on Netflix before it leaves in July should
be at the top of your to-do list.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:08.720
Because it's going:

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.200
"Hasta la vista, baby."

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:16.500
Vince Vaughn and Owen Wilson star in Wedding
Crashers as best buds and partners in crime

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.400
who have perfected the art of crashing weddings
and wooing women.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:23.860
In a hilarious montage, the film quickly chronicles
the pair's most successful wedding season

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.099
ever, then brings the audience up to speed
on their riskiest mission yet: sneaking into

00:04:28.099 --> 00:04:31.350
the wedding of a daughter of the U.S. Secretary
of the Treasury.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.930
Featuring more one-liners than we can quote
here and an absolutely hysterical performance

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:39.520
by Will Ferrell, Wedding Crashers is the epitome
of R-rated, mid-2000s comedies.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.880
